{
  "name": "vector_light_indoor_level",
  "saveFile": "minimal_colony.rws",
  "description": "Is a sealed interior brighter than vanilla? That is the failure every \u00a727 composition has to answer for \u2014 epic #145 rejected drawing our model over vanilla's at 6 L* over \u2014 and it is the one question the doorway scenes cannot ask. A room with a one-cell gap in its wall is an OUTDOOR room as far as RimWorld is concerned, roofed or not, so it reads sky and never tests the indoor level at all. This room is a sealed 15x15 box with no gap and no door, roofed explicitly with SetRoof because walls alone do not roof anything here, lit by one torch at midnight, with two interior stubs so the mask still has shadows to carve while the level is judged. Four arms: vanilla, the mask alone, the mask plus the shipped flat beam, and phase 6. In a sealed room our polygon can see every cell vanilla's flood reached, so the two models agree everywhere and a self-limiting max must add essentially NOTHING \u2014 this is the purest test of that property there is, and the arm to distrust is any that comes out bright.",
